# Each ignored CVE MUST have a VEX justification comment on the line directly
# above it. The policy is ENFORCED in CI by scripts/lint-trivyignore.py
# (build-and-scan.yml "Validate .trivyignore policy" pre-scan gate): an entry
# whose preceding line is missing, malformed, or carries an expired/absent
# expires= date fails the job.
# Format: # VEX: <status> - <justification> expires=YYYY-MM-DD
# Allowed statuses: not_affected, false_positive, will_not_fix
# expires= is mandatory and must be a future date (>= today, UTC).
#
# Example:
# VEX: not_affected - This component is not reachable in our configuration expires=2026-12-31
# CVE-2024-XXXXX

# No active suppressions.
#
# History (2026-06-01): the prior waivers (CVE-2026-0861 glibc, CVE-2026-28390
# openssl) covered unpatched OS CVEs in the old gcr.io/distroless/nodejs20-debian12
# base. The runtime base was switched to cgr.dev/chainguard/node (Wolfi-based),
# which ships fixed packages and scans 0 HIGH/CRITICAL, so those waivers no
# longer apply and were removed rather than left as dead entries. The four
# OpenSSL libssl3 CVEs that were blocking (CVE-2026-31789, -28387, -28388,
# -28389) are RESOLVED by the base-image change, not suppressed.
